% Generated with knitr; edit this Rnw source, not the output tex.
<<bootstrap-data, include=FALSE>>=
x <- c(1, 2, 3)
n <- length(x)
x_bar <- mean(x)
@

\section{Bootstrap calculation}
This chunk implements Algorithm~\ref{alg:bootstrap-mean}. The seed fixes the
random-number stream used for this demonstration. With only three
observations, the empirical distribution has very limited support; the
bootstrap interval below illustrates computation rather than reliable
coverage for a scientific application.

<<bootstrap-mean>>=
set.seed(20260927)
B <- 2000L
alpha <- 0.05
boot_mean <- replicate(
  B, mean(sample(x, size = n, replace = TRUE))
)
quantile(boot_mean,
         probs = c(alpha / 2, 1 - alpha / 2), names = FALSE)
@

Report the seed, the number of resamples, the interval method, and software
versions in a reproducible
analysis. These bootstrap resamples are distinct from the independently
generated datasets used to estimate repeated-sampling coverage in a simulation
study.


\section{A figure generated by R}
Figure~\ref{fig:bootstrap-distribution} displays the empirical cumulative
distribution of the bootstrap means from Algorithm~\ref{alg:bootstrap-mean}.
Its steps reflect the limited support of the three-observation sample.
The vertical lines identify the observed mean and percentile endpoints.

<<figure-caption, include=FALSE>>=
bootstrap_caption <- paste(
  "Empirical cumulative distribution of 2,000 bootstrap means from",
  "the observations 1, 2, and 3, using seed 20260927.",
  "The dotted line marks the observed mean of 2; dashed lines mark",
  "the 95 percent percentile interval endpoints of 1 and 3.",
  "This small-sample example illustrates computation, not reliable coverage."
)
knitr::opts_template$set(bootstrap_figure = list(
  fig.cap = bootstrap_caption,
  fig.scap = "Empirical cumulative distribution of bootstrap means",
  fig.width = 6, fig.height = 4, out.width = "\\linewidth",
  fig.align = "center", fig.pos = "tbp"
))
@

<<bootstrap-distribution, opts.label='bootstrap_figure'>>=
endpoints <- quantile(
  boot_mean, probs = c(alpha / 2, 1 - alpha / 2), names = FALSE
)
plot(ecdf(boot_mean),
     main = "", xlab = "Bootstrap sample mean",
     ylab = "Empirical cumulative probability",
     verticals = TRUE, do.points = FALSE, xlim = c(0.8, 3.2))
abline(v = x_bar, lty = 3)
abline(v = endpoints, lty = 2, col = "blue")
legend("topleft", c("Observed mean", "Percentile endpoints"),
       lty = c(3, 2), col = c("black", "blue"), bty = "n")
@

Figure~\ref{fig:bootstrap-distribution} and its caption are generated by
knitr from this chunk. The chunk name supplies the figure label, and
\verb|\ref| supplies its number in the text. The shorter caption appears in
the list of figures; the full caption explains the data and line styles.


